{"content":[{"c":["KARKOR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City in the Transjordan where Gideon attacked the armies of the two Midianite kings, Zebah and Zalmunna (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.10","r":"Judg.8.10","rawR":"Judg.8.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.10","value":"Judg.8.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 8:10"},"). Indications of its location are sketchy. ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.11","r":"Judg.8.11","rawR":"Judg.8.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.11","value":"Judg.8.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Judges 8:11"}," places it east of Nobah and Jog-behah, a town identified with Jubeiah, which is seven miles (11.3 kilometers) northwest of Amman in Jordan. A more feasible site is in the vicinity of ancient Succoth (Tell Dier ‘Alla) and Penuel (Tell edh-Dhahab esh-Sherqiyeh), both assigned to Gad’s tribe in Gilead."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Karkor","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 8:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.10","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.10","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.10"},{"anchorText":"Judges 8:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.11","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.11","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8da2c6bb978fbfb99fcc9766f793781d7bb3306bd0f9545528b783b40a04cc44","sourceItemName":"Karkor","sourceItemOrder":15,"sourceMember":"Articles/K.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Karkor","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Karkor","title":"Karkor","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}